{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Segment, RudderStack and Customer.io Data Pipelines each take the same batch call of the Segment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spec, at endpoints of their own. One encoder, "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":", writes it, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory for each fills in the endpoint and how the key travels:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" posts to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/v1\/batch"},{"type":"text","text":" of the workspace’s region ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), with the write key as HTTP Basic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authentication’s user name and an empty password."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" posts to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/v1\/batch"},{"text":" of your data plane URL, with the write key the same way.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" posts to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Pipelines API’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the workspace’s region (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), with the key as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bearer token and ","type":"text"},{"code":"X-Strict-Mode: 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each splits a batch to the spec’s limits ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"): 2,500 calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 500 KB a request, and under 32 KB a call, which all three accept. A batch with no record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. Each retries no response, a 5xx, 408"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The key goes in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization"},{"type":"text","text":" header field, never in the body. It is a public client key:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Segment’s and RudderStack’s write keys, and Customer.io’s public keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pk_…"},{"type":"text","text":"), ship in their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vendors’ own app and web libraries, and they let a client send data to the source and read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s private keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sk_…"},{"type":"text","text":") reach every Customer.io API, deleting people included, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the factory throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError\/privateKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for one. Each factory throws for an empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), RudderStack’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a data plane URL that isn’t a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":" URL, and Customer.io’s for a public key of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other region."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A region has no default. Segment and Customer.io keep a workspace’s data in the US or the EU, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events posted to the other region’s endpoint don’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes a track call of an anonymous user. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher; a record with no session is sent under its own record identifier. No","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call or traits are sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a redelivered record keeps, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. The standard context","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"goes in the spec’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fields (","type":"text"},{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"device","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"network","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"device.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"advertisingId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call’s "},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which Segment takes in place of the request’s address, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it records none. RudderStack fills in a "},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from the request unless the call has one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"even beside "},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and passes it on to its destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Customer.io’s references don’t say whether "},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the place"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the address it reads from an HTTP request, so it may still record the request’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each endpoint counts a user per "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is each record sent without a session. On a plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out under the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send. Segment deduplicates calls by "},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops most duplicates within about 24 hours, not all, so one it stored before the app ended is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most likely not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s API references don’t say whether"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they deduplicate, so such a record may be stored twice there."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one named as one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User Deleted"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User Suppressed"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Device Deleted"},{"text":" and the rest), one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for a call. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":", and the encoder logs a notice for each semantic event name in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan when the destination is made.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Segment answers 200 for every request but one too large or not JSON, so a wrong region, a write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key of no source, or a batch of more calls than it takes may be answered 200 with nothing stored."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Check the source’s debugger after setting the destination up. RudderStack answers a wrong write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key with 401, and Customer.io, in strict mode, with 401 too, so the destination reports those. In"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"strict mode Customer.io refuses a whole batch for one bad call, so the encoder leaves out each call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io documents refusing; a 400 for anything else drops the whole request."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude or Mixpanel, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SegmentSpecEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: segment)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what each endpoint receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Segment","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Segment"},{"title":"Sending to RudderStack","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-RudderStack"},{"title":"Sending to Customer.io Data Pipelines","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Customerio-Data-Pipelines"},{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}],"title":"SegmentSpecEncoding","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Send records as Segment-spec track calls to Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/CustomerIOSetupError/privateKey":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"privateKey","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError\/privateKey","kind":"symbol","title":"CustomerIOSetupError.privateKey","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/customeriosetuperror\/privatekey","abstract":[{"text":"The key is a private key (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sk_..."},{"text":"), not a public one (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pk_..."},{"text":"). A private key reaches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every Customer.io API, deleting and suppressing people included, and must not ship in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/rudderstack(writekey:dataplane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","title":"rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the RudderStack source of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"writeKey"},{"type":"text","text":", through the data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plane at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dataPlane"},{"type":"text","text":", through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"rudderStack"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"writeKey"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"dataPlane"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URL"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"transport"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding21RudderStackSetupErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RudderStackSetupError"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder":{"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"text":" of the Segment spec’s batch call, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to Segment, RudderStack, Customer.io Data Pipelines, or another endpoint that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes Segment’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecbatchencoder","role":"symbol"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSetupError":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError","title":"SegmentSetupError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"couldn’t make a destination."}],"url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentsetuperror","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentSetupError","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSpecEncodingError":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecEncodingError"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecEncodingError"}],"title":"SegmentSpecEncodingError","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecencodingerror","role":"symbol"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/RudderStackSetupError":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/rudderstacksetuperror","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RudderStackSetupError"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError","title":"RudderStackSetupError","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"couldn’t make a destination.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RudderStackSetupError"}]},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/CustomerIORegion":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CustomerIORegion","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","kind":"symbol","title":"CustomerIORegion","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/customerioregion","abstract":[{"text":"The region of a Customer.io workspace, which decides the Pipelines API endpoint its events are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"posted to.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CustomerIORegion","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/segment(writekey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","title":"segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the Segment source of "},{"code":"writeKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", in a workspace in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"region","type":"codeVoice"},{"ty